@startuml
title One token, three rules: how `!` resolves to PRep, POut or POutAsync

skinparam backgroundColor #FEFEFE
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #374151
skinparam ArrowThickness 1.2
skinparam activity {
  BorderColor #1F2937
  FontColor #111827
  DiamondBorderColor #1F2937
  DiamondFontColor #111827
}

start

:the lexer yields ""TokenKind::Fixed(\"!\")"";

if (is there a completed left operand?) then (**no** — `!` is in LEADING position)
  :**PRep** — replication ""!p""\nProc rule index 6; <<#DCFCE7>>
  note right #DCFCE7
    Dispatched by the PREFIX table of the
    ""Proc"" category (src_idx 0): the pair
    ""(0u16, 6u16)"" maps to the leading
    literal ""!"" in the generated WPDA.

    ""Proc"" declares NO infix, postfix or
    mixfix entry for ""!"" at all — its
    ""infix_bp_proc"", ""postfix_bp_proc"" and
    ""mixfix_bp_proc"" tables are empty.
  end note
  stop
else (**yes** — of category ""Name"")
endif

:consult the ""Name"" category's continuation tables\n(src_idx 1) — BOTH have an entry for ""!"";

split
  :""mixfix_bp_name(\"!\") = [(2, 0, 3)]""\nleft_bp 2, result category ""Proc"", rule 3;
  :candidate **POut**\n""n \"!\" m \".\" p"" — SYNCHRONOUS,\ncarries a continuation; <<#FEF3C7>>
split again
  :""infix_bp_name(\"!\") = [(4, 5, 0, 4)]""\nleft_bp 4, right_bp 5, result ""Proc"", rule 4;
  :candidate **POutAsync**\n""n \"!\" m"" — ASYNCHRONOUS,\nno continuation; <<#FEF3C7>>
end split

:BOTH candidates stay live —\nthe parser does NOT commit at ""!""; <<#EDE9FE>>

note right #EDE9FE
  ""POutAsync""'s syntax is a proper PREFIX of
  ""POut""'s: the two agree on ""n ! m"" and
  diverge only afterwards. No amount of
  precedence can separate them at the ""!"",
  so the WPDA carries both alternatives and
  lets the INPUT decide. This is the house
  rule — never disambiguate early.
end note

if (what follows the second ""Name""?) then (a ""."" and a process)
  :**POut** wins — ""c!c.0""; <<#DCFCE7>>
  note right #DCFCE7
    Pinned by ""pi_output_prefix_parses""
    (languages/tests/pi.rs:144).
  end note
  stop
else (the operand ends)
  :**POutAsync** wins — ""c!c""; <<#DCFCE7>>
  note right #DCFCE7
    Pinned by ""pi_comm_async_fires""
    (languages/tests/pi.rs:275), whose
    subject is ""{ in(c,y).0 | c!c }"".
  end note
  stop
endif

legend right
|= Colour |= Meaning |
|<#DCFCE7> green | a committed surface rule |
|<#FEF3C7> amber | a live candidate, not yet committed |
|<#EDE9FE> violet | the parser state in which ambiguity is deliberately preserved |
endlegend

@enduml
